                                        Page 47
     
     ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ
      ° InterBBS League Configuration °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°
     ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ
     
     InterBBS play adds a whole new dimension to Barren Realms Elite.  By
     creating a "league" of bulletin board systems all playing the same game,
     you can "connect" them together to allow play inter-BBS.  This allows
     players to compete against each other on a global scale.
     
     Setting up InterÄBBS warfare in Barren Realms Elite involves a very
     simple process.  In general (with exceptions), it requires an external
     netmail system such as Frontdoor, Binkley, or Dbridge.  However, other
     types of packet transfer have been used such as e-mail and FTP via the
     internet.
     
     Following these steps should make the process of becoming a part of an
     InterBBS Interactive Barren Realms Elite game as easy as possible.
     
     
         1.   Decide whether you would like to create your own league or join
              another.  If you have not had any experience with InterBBS
              games, it is a good idea to consider first joining another.
     
              A "League" is a set of systems which are all linked together,
              with a "League Coordinator" being the sysop of the system in
              charge.  It is that person that you should contact about
              joining a game.  They are always BBS #1 in a List of BBSes in
              the game.
     
              Once you have contacted the central BBS, you will receive a
              BRNODES.DAT file.  Check to make sure your BBS is in it with
              the correct node number.
     
              IF YOU CHOOSE TO CREATE YOUR OWN LEAGUE, THERE IS ADDITIONAL
              INFORMATION BELOW.  Please see the section on becoming a league
              coordinator.
     
     
         2.   At this point you should have, or be expecting, to get an
              BRNODES.DAT file.  You need to create a BBS.CFG file in one of
              the following ways:
     
                   Method #1 - Run "BRE SETUPINTERBBS" and input all of the
                   necessary information.  If you do not know the League
                   Number yet, you will need to modify this to join the game
                   (find out from your League Coordinator)
     
                   Method #2 - Create it yourself.  Look at SAMPLES\BBS.SAM
                   for more details about the format - it is extremely
                   simple.




                                        Page 48
     
         3.   You now have an BRNODES.DAT and BBS.CFG file.  You should find
              out from your League Coordinator whether or not you need to
              create a ROUTE.CFG file.  Your league may already take care of
              routing in the BRNODES.DAT through a HOST routing system, in
              which case you may skip this step.
     
              Otherwise, look at the SAMPLES\ROUTE.SAM for more information
              about how to set up your own routing information.  Note that
              even if you are letting the League Coordinator set up the
              proper routing, if you want mail to be placed CRASH or HOLD,
              you will need to set that in your ROUTE.CFG file.
     
         4.   Run "BRE PLANETARY" to your daily maintenance.  You may also
              run this more often in order to process data several times a
              day.  Alternatively, you may run "BRE FULL" instead of "BRE"
              when users play and the game will process data when the user is
              playing.
     
              Run "BRE SCORES" in your daily maintenance to ensure the daily
              creation of the InterBBS scores files.
     
     
         5.   You're almost done.  You should have the BRNODES.DAT, BBS.CFG,
              and ROUTE.CFG (optional) files now.  Run "BRE TEST" and make
              sure everything looks OK.  If so, you should be all set.  Enjoy
              the game!  If not, you'll need to backtrack to see what
              happened.  Here are some possible problems:
     
              Problem: 
     
              Not a member of InterBBS League
     
     
              Solutions:
     
              Check to make sure BBS.CFG and BRNODES.DAT are properly named
              and in the main Barren Realms Elite directory
              
              Check to make sure your Node Number in each of those files
              matches exactly
     
     
              Problem:
     
              The routing from BRE TEST is not what I want
     
     
              Solutions:
     
              If you're using the HOST system defined by your League
              Coordinator, contact him or her and let him know
     
              If you're using the ROUTE.CFG file, check to make sure you
              typed everything in properly.
                                        Page 49
     
     Becoming a League Coordinator
     
     In addition to the above steps, as League Coordinator, you will be
     responsible for creating and maintaining the BRNODES.DAT file and the
     league in general.
     
     This involves adding new systems, deleting old ones, checking the
     routing, and ensuring fairness.  For information on the format of the
     BRNODES.DAT file, see SAMPLES\NODEFORM.INF.  We highly recommend you use
     the HOST routing method so that other systems do not need to worry about
     their own routing.
     
     You will also need to be sure to select a League Number between 1 and
     999.  This number identifies your league so BBSes running multiple games
     can be kept separated.  It is OK to have 2 leagues with the same number,
     but no single system can be a member of both of those leagues.
     
     
     Transferring Coordinatorship
     
     If you would like to hand over the job of coordinatorship in your league
     to another BBS, you must copy the COORD.KEY file to the BRE directory of
     the new BBS and make him BBS #1 in the BRNODES.DAT file.































                                        Page 50
     
     Sample InterBBS Configuration Files
     
     The following pages outline the various configuration files required for
     InterBBS play.  Each section also includes a sample file that may be
     exported as text for editing.
     
     Refer to the section on setting up InterBBS game play for information on
     how to begin setting up an InterBBS league.














































                                        Page 51
     
     BBS.CFG
     
     This file holds basic information about your BBS while it is in the
     league.  BBS.CFG should be located in your main Barren Realms Elite
     directory:
     
     
         Line 1
         Sysop Name
     
         Line 2
         BBS or Nation Name - This is used only to identify your system in
         the game, so use whatever you like - to make others see the selected
         name, request that it be placed in the Nodelist in place of the BBS
         name.
     
         Line 3
         NodeNumber with Zone:Net/Node.
     
         Line 4
         Your Front End Incoming FILE Directory
     
         Line 5
         Your NetMail Directory
     
         Line 6
         League number - Must be the same throughout the league.  This can be
         any number between 1 and 999.  If a BBS chooses to be involved in
         two leagues, they must use different League Numbers, or Barren
         Realms Elite won't know which data packets are for which game.
     
         Line 7
         Your Front End Mailer.  This should be one of the following:
         FRONTDOOR, BINKLEY, DBRIDGE, INTERMAIL, DBRIDGEOLD, OTHER or NONE. 
         
         If you wish to run BRE PLANETARY more than once a day, you MUST be
         running Front Door, Binkleyterm, D'Bridge, or Intermail.
     
         D'Bridge 1.51 and below do not support the necessary features for
         BRE to allow multiple files per day to be transferred, and you must
         therefore use the "DBRIDGEOLD" setting.  If you run D'Bridge 1.51-
         or OTHER, then you will only be able to run BRE PLANETARY once a
         day.
     
         Also, many systems are running BRE *without* a mail system
         completely (no idea how, but they have succeeded!).  You can use the
         NONE setting if you delete files after they are sent.  Selecting
         NONE will *not* create a .MSG file.






                                        Page 52
     
     John Doe
     My BBS
     1:222/333
     C:\FD\FILES
     C:\FD\NETMAIL
     999
     FRONTDOOR















































                                        Page 53
     
     BRNODES.DAT
     
     This file outlines all of the nodes in a particular league.  IF YOU ARE
     NOT THE LEAGUE COORDINATOR, YOU SHOULD NOT BE MODIFYING THE BRNODES.DAT
     FILE IN ANY CASE.  This file should also be stored in your main Barren
     Realms Elite directory.
     
     
         BBS 1 Line 1
         BBS Number with optional HOST routing system.  Number assigned to
         any BBS in the game.  BBS #1 is the manager of the game and will
         automatically send out BRNODES.DAT update to the BBS's.  The HOST
         routing system is explained below.
     
         BBS 1 Line 2
         BBS or Nation Name.  The Name of the BBS or Nation.  To make the
         game more enjoyable for the players, we recommend that BBSes create
         "nation" names such as "USA" or "Canada" or "Solaria" instead of
         their BBS name to create a game atmosphere.  Each BBS, of course,
         should choose a different name.
     
         BBS 1 Line 3
         Zone:Net/Node Number.  Your FrontEnd Zone:Net/Node Number.  This
         game should work on any fido-net compatible network.
     
         BBS 1 Line 4
         City
     
         BBS 1 Line 5
         Two Letter State Code
     
         BBS 1 Line 6
         Country
     
     A blank Line separates entries in the node list
     
         BBS 2 Line 1
         BBS Number with optional HOST routing system
     
         BBS 2 Line 2
         BBS or Nation Name
     
         BBS 2 Line 3
         Zone:Net/Node Number
     
         BBS 2 Line 4
         City
     
         BBS 2 Line 5
         Two Letter State Code
     
         BBS 2 Line 6
         Country2
     
         ...
                                        Page 54
     
     Host Routing System
     
     If your league uses a centralized routing system with Hubs, the safest
     and simplest way of maintaining this routing is by having the League
     Coordinator manage it.
     
     If BBS 2 has systems 3,4, and 8 sending all of their data to it, you
     should have, for BBS #2, the following for its first line:
     
     2 HOST 3 4 8
     My BBS
     1:222/333
     etc.
     
     
     Suppose this is the routing structure:
     
                                    BBS #1
                                  /        \
                               BBS #2     BBS #4
                             / |  |  \    |  |  \
                            3  5  7  8    6  9  11
                                                 |
                                                 10
     
     BBSes 3, 5, 7, 8, 6, 9, and 10 would not be HOSTs and would therefore
     not have any routing information.
     
     BBS #2 would list 3, 5, 7, and 8 after it.
     
     BBS #4 would list 6, 9, and 10 only.  BBS #11 would list only 10.
     
     BBS #1 would list only 2 and 4.
     
     So the entire nodelist would have [Line #1 shown only for each BBS]:
     
     1 HOST 2 4
     2 HOST 3 5 7 8
     3
     4 HOST 6 9 11
     5
     6
     7
     8
     9
     10
     11 HOST 10
     
     Barren Realms Elite will then determine the necessary data routing for
     each BBS.




                                        Page 55
     
     1
     My BBS
     1:222/333
     Some City
     ST
     USA
     
     2
     Another BBS
     1:444/555
     A Big City
     ST
     USA
     
     3
     Yet Another BBS
     1:999/111
     Somewhere
     ST
     CAN
     
     ...
































                                        Page 56
     
     ROUTE.CFG
     
     This file holds information regarding the routing of interBBS packets. 
     If your League Coordinator is managing your routing through HOST routing
     system in the nodelist, you do not need a ROUTE.CFG file.  However, any
     information in this file will override anything else assumed by the
     BRNODES.DAT file.  You may put these lines in this file at any location
     and in any order.
     
     Again, ROUTE.CFG must be stored in the main BRE Directory  The following
     may be used in the routing configuration file.
     
     
         ROUTE
     
         If you wish to route data destined to a particular node to another
         node, use the following format:
     
              ROUTE 5 10
     
         This will route all mail for BBS #5 in your BRNODES.DAT to BBS #10
         ROUTE also supports "*" as the first parameter to represent "ALL":
     
              ROUTE * 8
     
         This will route ALL mail for ANY BBS through BBS #8.  Using ROUTE 5
         5 after a "Route * #" command will restore BBS #5 to Direct
     
     
         CRASH PRIORITY MAIL
     
         By default, all BRE mail is set to "Normal Priority" in your mailer. 
         If you wish for BRE to set mail up to CRASH Priority, use the
         following format:
     
              CRASH 5
     
         This will put all mail to BBS #5 as CRASH Mail CRASH * with set
         crash priority to ALL nodes
     
     
         HOLD MAIL
     
         The format to put mail on HOLD is the same as CRASH.
     
              HOLD 5
     
              HOLD * with put mail on hold to ALL nodes






                                        Page 57
     
         NORMAL MAIL
     
         The format to put mail on NORMAL mode, cancelling crash & hold
         priorities.
     
              NORMAL 5
              NORMAL * with put mail on NORMAL for ALL nodes















































                                        Page 58
     
     Local InterBBS Setup
     
     Many sysops are unwilling to setup the InterBBS Gaming System, are
     unsure of its workings, or are unwilling to connect to another system. 
     This file explains how to set up several local games to be
     interconnected so you may essentially run an "InterBBS Local Game".
     
     This can be especially interesting if you have a large number of players
     on the board who wish to form "teams" and fight, etc.
     
     See the INTERBBS.DOC for basic information on how to set up your
     BRNODES.DAT and BBS.CFG files.
     
     
         Setting up BRNODES.DAT
     
         Each game should have a different Nodelist number and name.  For
         simplicity, it is recommended that you use 1:1/1 for the first game,
         1:1/2 for the second, and so forth.
     
     
         Setting up BBS.CFG
     
         For all games (2..n), the INBOUND FILES directory should be:
     
              [GAME(N-1)]\OUTBOUND
     
         For game #1, the INBOUND FILES directory should be:
     
              [GAME(N)]\OUTBOUND
     
         For example: Suppose you have a 4-game setup in directories C:\BRE1,
         C:\BRE2, C:\BRE3, and C:\BRE4.
     
              Game            Inbound File Directory
     
              1               C:\BRE4\OUTBOUND
              2               C:\BRE1\OUTBOUND
              3               C:\BRE2\OUTBOUND
              4               C:\BRE3\OUTBOUND
     
     
         Setting up ROUTE.CFG
     
         All systems should route data to the next system, with the last
         routing all data to game #1.  For a 4-game system, you should have
         the following:
     
              Game 1 should have a route.cfg with: "ROUTE * 2"
              Game 2 should have a route.cfg with: "ROUTE * 3"
              Game 3 should have a route.cfg with: "ROUTE * 4"
              Game 4 should have a route.cfg with: "ROUTE * 1"


                                        Page 59
     
         This basically produces a file circle.  Run BRE PLANETARY on each
         system 1Äx in order, and all the necessary information will be
         properly transmitted between systems.  Running this cycle twice will
         produce immediate results of all attacks, etc.


















































                                        Page 60
     
